ThetoString()method returns a standard ISO string.

APlainTimevalue is formatted as a time string.

APlainDateTimevalue includes both date and time.

AZonedDateTimestring includes the offset and time zone.

You can control how much detail to include.

For example, you can hide seconds or milliseconds.

You can choose how many decimal digits to include.

UsetoLocaleString()to format a value using the user's locale.

The output depends on the chosen locale.

UseIntl.DateTimeFormatwhen you need more control over the output.

You can format aPlainDateTimewith both date and time options.

TheIntl.DateTimeFormat()methoddoes not
accept a Temporal.ZonedDateTimeobject as input.

This design choice prevents conflicts between the time zone held by the
ZonedDateTime and the time zone defined in the formatter.

The best solution is to usetoLocaleString()instead.

### Code Snippets

```
const date = Temporal.PlainDate.from("2026-05-17");
let text = date.toString();

---

2026-05-17

---

const time = Temporal.PlainTime.from("14:30:15");
let text = time.toString();

---

14:30:15

---

const dateTime = Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("2026-05-17T14:30:15");
let text = dateTime.toString();

---

2026-05-17T14:30:15

---

const zoned = Temporal.ZonedDateTime.from("2026-05-17T14:30:15[Europe/Oslo]");
let text = zoned.toString();

---

2026-05-17T14:30:15+01:00[Europe/Oslo]
or:
2026-05-17T14:30:15+02:00[Europe/Oslo]

---

const time = Temporal.PlainTime.from("14:30:15.123");
let text = time.toString({ smallestUnit: "minute" });

---

14:30

---

const time = Temporal.PlainTime.from("14:30:15.123456789");
let text = time.toString({ fractionalSecondDigits: 3 });

---

14:30:15.123

---

const date = Temporal.PlainDate.from("2026-05-17");
let text_us = date.toLocaleString("en-US");
let text_de = date.toLocaleString("de-DE");

---

const zoned = Temporal.ZonedDateTime.from("2026-05-17T14:30:15+01:00[Europe/Oslo]");
let text = zoned.toLocaleString("en-US", {
dateStyle: "full",
timeStyle: "short"
});

---

const date = Temporal.PlainDate.from("2026-05-17");
const formatter = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-US", {
year: "numeric",
month: "long",
day: "numeric"
});
let text = formatter.format(date);

---

February 17, 2026

---

const dateTime = Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("2026-05-17T14:30:15");
const formatter = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-GB", {
year: "numeric",
month: "short",
day: "numeric",
hour: "2-digit",
minute: "2-digit"
});
let text = formatter.format(dateTime);

---

const zoned = Temporal.ZonedDateTime.from("2026-05-17T14:30:15+01:00[Europe/Oslo]");
let text = zoned.toLocaleString("en-US", {
dateStyle: "full",
timeStyle: "short"
});
```
